Findings:

- Line 163: `git checkout -- page` restores from the index, not HEAD. Exact input: HEAD has `p.html=A`, staged index has `p.html=B`, worktree has `p.html=C`, and `PAGE_MAP` includes `p.html`; consequence: the “committed copy” baseline measured at line 195 is `B`, not committed `A`.

- Line 193: `restore_from_git(page)` return value is ignored. Exact input: `PAGE_MAP` includes an untracked `p.html`; `git checkout -- p.html` exits nonzero, but line 195 still measures the worktree; consequence: the guard reads the wrong copy after restore failure.

- Lines 180-181: the idempotency guard treats any ledger key as done. Exact input: `{"done":{"p.html":{"state":"PREDICTION FAILED"}}}`; consequence: reruns skip a failed page as already complete.

- Lines 183-184: zero is conflated with absent. Exact input: `--limit=0`; consequence: the script builds all todo pages instead of none.

- Lines 145 and 219: “byte-identical” is implemented as character-count inequality. Exact input: before page text `id="paper">A`, after page text `id="paper">B` with the same length; consequence: a changed page can fail the “not byte-identical” check, while byte identity itself is never compared.

- Line 218: “earlier” allows equality. Exact input: before `first_sentence_at=5`, after `first_sentence_at=5`; consequence: no earlier reach is reported as passing.

- Line 50: the estimate regex drops a negative point-estimate sign. Exact input: before `-0.42 (-0.70 to -0.10)`, after `0.42 (-0.70 to -0.10)`; consequence: an effect-direction reversal passes `1_nothing_lost`.

- Lines 67-68 and 217: failed or empty transcript extraction becomes `want=[]`, and `all([])` passes. Exact input object: `{"results":{"by_outcome":{"x":{}}}}` with a page that carried a transcript before and drops it after; consequence: transcript preservation is vacuous.

- Lines 142 and 217: transcript comparison reads HTML as text, normalizing line endings. Exact input stored transcript `a\nb`, delivered bytes `a\r\nb`; consequence: byte identity is reported even though delivered bytes differ.

No merged-cell/tabulation defect found in this module.  
COULD NOT DETERMINE corpus-specific selector underreach without `PAGE_MAP.json`, object JSON files, rendered pages, and `build_tabbed.py`.
